<title>UK: World Bank adds 2.0 bln rand to zero-coupon bond.</title>
<headline>World Bank adds 2.0 bln rand to zero-coupon bond.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-03-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following bond has been increased to four billion rand from two billion rand, lead manager J.P. Morgan said.</p>
<p> BORROWER   WORLD BANK</p>
<p> AMT ** 4.0 BLN RAND  COUPON     ZERO	MATURITY    01.APR.22</p>
<p> TYPE	 STRAIGHT  ISS PRICE  4.03	PAY DATE    01.APR.97</p>
<p> FULL FEES  0.35	REOFFER    3.805     SPREAD	=</p>
<p> MOODY	AAA	 LISTING    LUX	 PAY FREQ    =</p>
<p> S&amp;P	  AAA	 DENOMS (K) 5-50-500  SALE LIMITS US/UK/ZA</p>
<p> NEG PLG    YES	 CRS DEFLT  YES	 FORCE MAJ   YES</p>
<p> GOV LAW    ENGLISH   HOME CTRY  SUPRA     TAX PROVS   STANDARD</p>
<p> MGT/UND    0.125     SELL CONC  0.225     PRAECIPUUM  =</p>
<p> NOTES	**ORIGINAL 2.0 BLN LAUNCHED 11.MAR AT 3.99</p>
<p>		ISSUED OFF MULTI-CURRENCY PROGRAMME</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7658</p>
